  "phrases": [
    {
      "scene": 1,
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.691083,
      "text": "Who creates your Java objects?"
    },
    {
      "scene": 2,
      "start": 1.891083,
      "end": 6.906625,
      "text": "Without Spring, your code creates a repository, then passes it into a service."
    },
    {
      "scene": 3,
      "start": 7.146625,
      "end": 15.099708,
      "text": "With Spring, you register bean definitions. The container uses them to create managed objects and wire their dependencies."
    },
    {
      "scene": 4,
      "start": 15.349708,
      "end": 19.923375,
      "text": "Here, the service bean asks for a repository. Spring supplies that bean."
    },
    {
      "scene": 5,
      "start": 20.163375,
      "end": 28.990625,
      "text": "Your application calls get bean to request the ready service. In our Java run, its repository is the same bean from the container."
    },
    {
      "scene": 6,
      "start": 29.250625,
      "end": 39.962667,
      "text": "Your app starts Spring with Config. Spring calls Config\u2019s bean methods, creates Repo, and wires Service. Your app retrieves the ready service. Managed beans only."
    },
    {
      "scene": 7,
      "start": 41.962667,
      "end": 43.053417,
      "text": "Thanks for watching."
    }
  ],
